10837	{"artifactId":"LLD-c96a97a204fac22b-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-c96a97a204fac22b-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-12T08:57:28.112Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The root cause the ISSUE states (every save writes the whole session with its transcript; list() reads every session in full) is what the design removes: saves append only new rows and replace a small head, and list() reads heads only.","evidence":"session-store.ts:195 `void memento.update(SESSION_PREFIX + session.id, session);` writes the whole ChatSession; list() at 241-248 calls get(id) for every indexed id and reads the full record only to take id/provider/title/updatedAtOf. The design's head file carries exactly those fields plus updatedAt, and the rows file takes the transcript, so both halves of the root cause and the ISSUE's 'history list should not need every transcript' are addressed. Migration covers 'existing sessions must keep working'. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts, docs/standalone/every-save-chat-session-rewrites-its-E20261012c96a97a2/ISSUE.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.2","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The design keeps a session from being lost or corrupted 'when a session is evicted', as the ISSUE's fix intent requires, including for a session object that is still held and saved after its files were removed.","evidence":"ISSUE.md fix intent: 'must not be lost or corrupted by the change, including when several windows share the same global state and when a session is evicted'. Today a save after eviction rewrites the whole record and re-adds the id (session-store.ts:195-206), so the session comes back complete. The design says a tracked object 'only ever appends, whatever else has happened to the files', keeps its count 'for as long as the object lives', and treats any size difference as 'another writer appended'. It names no case for a rows file that is missing or smaller than the recorded size. So after eviction (by another window, or by this store while a non-current turn still holds the object — turn-lifecycle.ts:326 and 338 call trySave(s) on such an object) the save appends only the rows beyond the count and writes a head: the session reappears holding only its newest rows, or none. The whole-file rewrite only triggers for an untracked object or a transcript shorter than its count, neither of which is this case. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts, docs/standalone/every-save-chat-session-rewrites-its-E20261012c96a97a2/ISSUE.md]","action":"Add a third whole-file case to 2.2: when the rows file is missing or smaller than the size this store recorded for the id (or the head is gone), write the object's full transcript through a temporary file and rename, then the head. Add an error-path entry and a unit test for 'held object saved after its files were evicted/removed'.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today extension.ts builds the chat store with createMementoChatSessionStore over context.globalState with a cap and an onEvict that removes output files, and sweeps output with a keep set of chatStore.list() ids; the wiring test pins these by text at lines 46, 255 and 256.","evidence":"extension.ts:446-454: `const chatStore = createMementoChatSessionStore({ memento: context.globalState, maxSessions: 200, onEvict: (id) => void chatOutput.remove(id)...` and `.sweep({ olderThanMs: CHAT_OUTPUT_MAX_AGE_MS, keep: new Set(chatStore.list().map((c) => c.id)) })`. extension-chat-wiring.test.ts:46 matches `createMementoChatSessionStore\\(\\{\\s*memento: context\\.globalState,\\s*maxSessions: \\d+,`, line 255 the onEvict, line 256 the sweep keep set. The session-store.ts header (line 7 'no local-JSON file') and the liveTurn comment (line 82 'Sessions live in globalState') read as the design quotes them. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/extension-chat-wiring.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The callers (chat-panel.ts, turn-lifecycle.ts) use the store only through the synchronous ChatSessionStore interface, so swapping the implementation in extension.ts needs no caller edits.","evidence":"Every non-test store use in vscode-plugin/src: chat-panel.ts:214 store.list(), 444 and 957 store.draft(), 965 store.get(), 999 store.save(), 1065 `if (deps.store.get(session.id) !== undefined) deps.store.save(session);`, plus trySaveSession (turn-lifecycle.ts:92-98, used at chat-panel.ts:141 and turn-lifecycle.ts:153). All are synchronous and none touches the memento or the key names. createMementoChatSessionStore is constructed in production only at extension.ts:446; the other occurrences are in tests (session-store.test.ts, chat-panel.test.ts, chat-shell.test.ts), which keep using the retained memento/in-memory store. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The edits to session-store.ts are complete as listed (two comments; createMementoChatSessionStore 'unchanged and kept'), with the migration in session-file-store.ts reading 'the existing insrc.chat.index and insrc.chat.session.<id> keys' and using isSession and updatedAtOf.","evidence":"session-store.ts:138-139 `const INDEX_KEY = 'insrc.chat.index'; const SESSION_PREFIX = 'insrc.chat.session.';`, line 141 `function isSession(v: unknown): v is ChatSession {` and line 154 `function updatedAtOf(s: ChatSession): string {` are all module-private (no `export`). The design puts migrateChatSessionsFromMemento and the head writer in a different file and relies on all four ('each indexed session that isSession accepts', head checks 'the same field checks as isSession', updatedAt 'as updatedAtOf computes today'), but lists only comment edits for session-store.ts. As written the new file cannot import them; the builder must either export them (an unlisted edit) or duplicate the key strings and checks, which would let the migration and the memento store drift. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts]","action":"Add to 3.5: export INDEX_KEY, SESSION_PREFIX, isSession and updatedAtOf from session-store.ts (or state that the migration lives in session-store.ts), so the keys and checks have one source.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The callers only ever push to a session's transcript (chat-panel.ts 238, 389, 812, 884, 896, 911), which is what makes append-by-count safe.","evidence":"A search of vscode-plugin/src outside tests for transcript.push/splice/pop/shift, `transcript.length =` and `transcript =` finds only pushes: chat-panel.ts:238, 389, 812, 884, 896, 911 and session-store.ts:252 (the memento store's own append). No caller reassigns or shortens a transcript; the only other writes are head fields (editMode at 998, mode at 1064, liveTurn/nativeSessionId in turn-lifecycle.ts). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The cap, eviction order and list() invariants the design promises match today's store: only a positive integer is a cap, the saved session is never evicted, oldest go first with onEvict per id, and list() sorts by updatedAt (last row's `at`, else createdAt) descending.","evidence":"session-store.ts:170-171 `deps.maxSessions !== undefined && deps.maxSessions >= 1 ? Math.floor(deps.maxSessions) : undefined`; 205-217 move the saved id to the end, evict from the front and call `deps.onEvict?.(id)` in a try/catch; 154-157 updatedAtOf; 247 the descending sort. savedAt-ordered eviction on a new head reproduces least-recently-saved order. One gap that does not break the invariant: the design does not say what savedAt the migration gives each head, and today's order lives only in the index array's position. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts]","action":"State in 2.4 that the migration assigns savedAt in index order (oldest first), so the first eviction after migration removes the same sessions the memento store would have.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion (ac1-ac4) is mapped to a test that observes the new behaviour and would fail without it, and the wiring test's pinned text is updated rather than left to break.","evidence":"The mapping in LLD-c96a97a204fac22b-s1.json (acceptanceMapping, ac1-ac4) ties ac1 to a recorded-call test (1,000 stored rows, one new row: bytes written must not grow), ac4 to 'list reads head files only, never a rows file', ac2 to migration tests including the failure-kept path, ac3 to the two-writer tests with a named mutation. Each asserts on recorded file calls, which the whole-record write at session-store.ts:195 could not satisfy. The current pins at extension-chat-wiring.test.ts:46 and 256 would fail after the rewiring, and the design replaces both. Caveats: the criteria texts themselves are not in ISSUE.md, so I checked the mapping against the fix intent; and no listed test covers a held object saved after its files were evicted (see the fix-targets-defect finding). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/extension-chat-wiring.test.ts, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-c96a97a204fac22b-s1.json]","action":"Add the eviction-then-save test alongside the fix for that finding.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":6,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-12T08:57:28.112Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
